  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Findings (200 digits, $\\theta=(1/3,-8/57)$; one chain point, two twist directions)\n\n**The zero-twist formula holds for [1,0,0] ⊗ [1,0,0]** with the general rules: poles $\\theta_s+\\{0,1\\}$, $c=3$, $E_\\lambda$ unchanged.\n- **Boxed formula (section 6).** $\\bar3$: physical limit $=361/35$ (same value as the 10 of the adjoint at this $t$), and $\\mathcal B_{\\bar3}/\\mathcal B_6$ matches to $8\\times10^{-23}$. $E_{\\bar3}/E_6=4$ is exactly what is required. With $c=2$ or $c=4$ it misses by 50% / 25%.\n- **Simplified $\\mathcal N''$ (section 7):** $-\\det\\mathcal N''=\\det\\mathcal N$ to 247 digits for both states.\n- **$c$ is not derived here.** The only pair of hw states has $a_1=0$, so the zero-twist $\\Delta T_2$ relation does not fix $\\kappa$. $c=3$ comes from the general rule and is tested only through the boxed formula (where $c\\pm1$ fail).\n\n**Open: the twisted identity is only O(ε)-exact for the fundamental (sections 4, 4b).**\n- Orthogonality holds ($4\\times10^{-181}$), but $\\det N/(c^{\\rm ref}\\Psi^{\\rm ref})\\cdot\\langle L|0\\rangle\\langle0|R\\rangle$ is not state-independent: spread $6.6\\times10^{-2},\\,6.7\\times10^{-3},\\,6.8\\times10^{-4}$ at $\\varepsilon=10^{-2},10^{-3},10^{-4}$, for all 36 row triples.\n- So some twist-dependent, state-dependent normalization factor (tending to 1 at zero twist) is missing from $c^{\\rm ref}$, $\\Psi^{\\rm ref}$ or the reference states in this case. Several twisted Q's have degree 0 here ($Q=z^{\\pm u}$), which may be where the L=1 normalization formulas stop applying. Not diagnosed further.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  }
 ],
